<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Woodchester 4-mth business up over 30 pct.</title>
<headline>Woodchester 4-mth business up over 30 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish financial services group Woodchester Investments Plc said on Thursday that new business in the first four months of this year exceeded 500 million Irish pounds, up more than 30 percent from the year-earlier period.</p>
<p>Woodchester said its non-performing loans as a percentage of total loans dropped to 2.3 percent at the end of April from 2.5 percent at the end of 1996.</p>
<p>The company said the economic outlook for all countries of operation remained favourable.</p>
<p>--Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9775</p>
